{"experiments":[  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Melanoma patients with BRAF V600E mutations have higher tumor mutational burden (TMB) and lower expression of the immune checkpoint gene PDCD1 compared to patients without BRAF mutations.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test whether BRAF V600E mutation status is associated with (1) higher TMB and (2) lower PDCD1 expression.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_mutations.csv, filter for mutations where Hugo_Symbol=='BRAF' and HGVSp_Short contains 'V600E'; label those patients as BRAF_V600E positive. 2. Compute per-patient TMB by counting total mutations, merge with mutation-derived BRAF status. 3. Load cleaned_gene_expression.csv, map PDCD1 (use mygene to map HUGO to Ensembl), extract PDCD1 expression per sample, compute per-patient median. 4. Merge TMB, PDCD1 expression, and BRAF status into a single dataframe; exclude missing data. 5. Compare TMB between BRAF_V600E positive and negative patients using Wilcoxon rank‐sum test. 6. Compare PDCD1 expression between groups by Wilcoxon test. 7. Adjust for age and gender in linear models if needed.","deliverables":"• Table of group sizes and descriptive statistics for TMB and PDCD1.  \n• Boxplots of TMB and PDCD1 expression by BRAF_V600E status.  \n• Wilcoxon test statistics and p-values for both comparisons.  \n• Optionally, linear regression summaries adjusting for age and gender."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Tumors with ulceration (ulceration_indicator='YES') exhibit significantly higher TMB than non-ulcerated tumors.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Assess whether ulcerated melanomas have greater mutational burden than non-ulcerated ones.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv and select patient_id and ulceration_indicator; recode ulceration_indicator into binary (YES vs NO), exclude missing. 2. Load cleaned_mutations.csv, compute per-patient TMB as mutation counts. 3. Merge TMB with ulceration status; exclude missing. 4. Compare TMB distributions between ulcerated and non-ulcerated groups using Wilcoxon rank‐sum test. 5. Visualize boxplot or violin plot of TMB by ulceration status.","deliverables":"• Summary table of median TMB by ulceration status.  \n• Boxplot/violin plot of TMB distributions.  \n• Wilcoxon test statistic and p-value."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Older age at diagnosis is positively correlated with tumor mutational burden in melanoma patients.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Quantify the association between patient age at diagnosis and TMB.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv, extract patient_id and age_at_diagnosis; exclude missing. 2. Load cleaned_mutations.csv, compute TMB per patient. 3. Merge TMB with age_at_diagnosis. 4. Compute Spearman’s rank correlation between age_at_diagnosis and TMB, report correlation coefficient and p-value. 5. Create scatter plot with age on x-axis and TMB on y-axis, overlay smoothing line.","deliverables":"• Spearman correlation coefficient and p-value.  \n• Scatter plot of age vs TMB with trend line."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"High expression of PD-L1 (CD274) modifies the effect of TMB on overall survival, such that patients with both high TMB and high CD274 have improved survival compared to other combinations.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test interaction between PD-L1 expression and TMB on overall survival.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv, compute survival time (days_to_death or days_to_last_followup) and event indicator. 2. Load cleaned_mutations.csv, compute per-patient TMB. 3. Load cleaned_gene_expression.csv, extract CD274 (PD-L1) expression per sample, compute per-patient median. 4. Merge survival, TMB, CD274 expression, age, gender; exclude missing. 5. Dichotomize TMB and CD274 at their medians into High/Low groups. 6. Fit a Cox proportional hazards model: Surv(time, event) ~ TMB_group * CD274_group + age + gender. 7. Extract hazard ratios and p-value for the interaction term. 8. Plot Kaplan–Meier curves for the four combinations (High/High, High/Low, Low/High, Low/Low).","deliverables":"• Cox model summary with hazard ratios and p-value for interaction.  \n• Forest plot of HRs including interaction.  \n• KM plots for the four TMB×CD274 groups with log-rank p-value."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Patients experiencing new tumor events after initial treatment have upregulated expression of invasion‐related genes MMP2 and MMP9 compared to those without events.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Identify whether post-treatment new tumor event status is associated with higher MMP2 and MMP9 expression.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv, extract patient_id and new_tumor_event_after_initial_treatment; recode to binary YES vs NO, exclude missing. 2. Load cleaned_gene_expression.csv, map HUGO symbols MMP2 and MMP9 to Ensembl IDs, extract per-sample expression, compute per-patient median for each gene. 3. Merge expression values with new tumor event status. 4. For each gene, compare expression between event vs no-event groups using Wilcoxon rank-sum tests. 5. Adjust p-values for multiple testing (two genes). 6. Visualize boxplots for each gene by event status.","deliverables":"• Summary statistics for MMP2 and MMP9 expression by group.  \n• Boxplots for MMP2 and MMP9.  \n• Wilcoxon test results and adjusted p-values."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Tumor mutational burden differs across racial groups, with non-white patients exhibiting lower TMB compared to white patients.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Examine racial disparities in TMB among melanoma patients.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv, extract patient_id and race; exclude missing or rare categories (retain White vs Non-White). 2. Load cleaned_mutations.csv, compute TMB per patient. 3. Merge TMB with race groups. 4. Compare TMB between White and Non-White groups using Wilcoxon test. 5. Optionally build a linear model TMB ~ race + age + gender to adjust for covariates. 6. Visualize boxplot of TMB by race category.","deliverables":"• Table of group sizes and median TMB by race.  \n• Boxplot of TMB by race.  \n• Wilcoxon test and, if applicable, linear model summary."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Patients with distant metastasis to lung or brain exhibit lower CD8A expression compared to patients without distant metastasis.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Test whether distant metastasis is associated with reduced CD8+ T cell infiltration (CD8A expression).",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv, extract patient_id and distant_metastasis_site; recode into binary Metastasis (Lung or brain) vs No Metastasis/other, exclude missing. 2. Load cleaned_gene_expression.csv, map CD8A to Ensembl ID, extract per-sample expression, compute per-patient median. 3. Merge CD8A expression with metastasis status. 4. Compare CD8A expression between metastasis vs non-metastasis groups using Wilcoxon test. 5. Visualize violin plot or boxplot of CD8A by group.","deliverables":"• Summary statistics for CD8A expression by metastasis status.  \n• Boxplot/violin plot of CD8A expression.  \n• Wilcoxon test statistic and p-value."  
    }  
  },  
  {  
    "hypothesis":"Unsupervised clustering of top 1,000 most variable genes in tumor expression data identifies patient subgroups with significantly different overall survival.",  
    "experiment_plan":{  
      "objective":"Discover molecular subtypes based on gene expression variability and test their prognostic relevance.",  
      "steps":"1. Load cleaned_gene_expression.csv; compute variance for each gene across samples, select top 1,000 most variable genes. 2. Standardize selected gene expressions and perform hierarchical clustering or consensus clustering to partition patients into k clusters (e.g., k=3). 3. Assign each patient to a cluster. 4. Load cleaned_clinical_data.csv; compute survival time/event. 5. Merge cluster labels with survival data. 6. Compare survival among clusters using Kaplan–Meier curves and log-rank test. 7. Optionally characterize clusters by average TMB or clinical features.","deliverables":"• Dendrogram or cluster assignment heatmap.  \n• KM curves for each cluster and log-rank p-value.  \n• Table of cluster sizes and median survival times.  \n• Summary of cluster characteristics (TMB, age, gender)."  
    }  
  }  
]}
